# 41. CORE RULES

```text
RULE 01
Every equipment has a unique Equipment_ID.

RULE 02
Equipment must be created through a valid recipe.

RULE 03
Equipment requires specific materials.

RULE 04
Equipment may require a specific Town Facility.

RULE 05
Equipment may require Town Level.

RULE 06
Equipment may require Master Level.

RULE 07
Hero Equipment may require Hero Level.

RULE 08
Hero Equipment may require a specific Hero Class.

RULE 09
Hero Equipment may require minimum Hero Stats.

RULE 10
Town Equipment primarily supports production,
crafting, storage, defense, and town development.

RULE 11
Medical Equipment primarily supports Hero recovery,
treatment, medicine production, and medical research.

RULE 12
Hero Equipment primarily supports combat,
survivability, skill performance, and expedition ability.

RULE 13
Equipment quality may be determined by Crafting RNG.

RULE 14
Equipment may have durability.

RULE 15
Damaged equipment can be repaired.

RULE 16
Hero Equipment can be upgraded, refined, and enchanted.

RULE 17
Equipment effects must be configurable.

RULE 18
Material prices and crafting costs are controlled
by the Economy System.

RULE 19
Higher-tier equipment requires higher-grade materials.

RULE 20
Advanced equipment should unlock progressively
through Town, Master, and Hero progression.

RULE 21
Medical equipment must be connected to the
Hero Injury / Recovery System.

RULE 22
Hero Equipment must be connected to the
Hero Loadout and Combat System.

RULE 23
Equipment should not directly bypass Floor progression.

RULE 24
Equipment progression should support,
not replace, Hero progression.

RULE 25
Equipment with Class Requirement cannot be used
at full effectiveness by an incompatible Hero.

RULE 26
Equipment obtained from special content may have
Bound Status and cannot always be traded.

RULE 27
Equipment Set bonuses are activated only when
the required number of pieces is equipped.

RULE 28
Consumable Equipment is removed from inventory
after use unless otherwise specified.
```

